sentences.l:
and no one has the courage to rage and nearer to approach,
but with javelins and with safe, from afar, shouts they press him;
he however, unafraid, delays towards all sides,
with his teeth gnashing, and from his back shakes off the spears;

sentences.t:
haud aliter, iustae quibus est Mezentius irae,
non ulli est animus stricto concurrere ferro;
missilibus longe et vasto clamore lacessunt:

sentences.l:
not otherwise, those to whom there is Mezentius for just anger,
not one has the heart with drawn steel to close;
with missiles from afar and with vast shouting they provoke him:

sentences.t:
Pedes et Lycius processerat Agis,
quem tamen haud expers Valerus virtutis avitae
deicit;

sentences.l:
On foot also the Lycian had come forward, Agis,
whom, however, not lacking in the courage of his forefathers, Valerus
throws down;
